  "content": {
    "id": "p77-q60-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "60",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x^2-4|x|+3$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p77-q60-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $f(x)=(|x|-1)(|x|-3)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use $x^2=|x|^2$ to obtain $f(x)=(|x|-1)(|x|-3)$.",
          "worked": "Since $|x|^2=x^2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}(|x|-1)(|x|-3)&=|x|^2-4|x|+3\\\\(|x|-1)(|x|-3)&=x^2-4|x|+3\\\\(|x|-1)(|x|-3)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p77-q60-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, or otherwise, solve $f(x)\\le 0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p77-q60-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-3\\le x\\le -1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 1\\le x\\le 3",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p77-q60-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The factored expression is non-positive when ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1\\le |x|\\le 3",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Put $u=|x|$, where $u\\ge0$. From part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}(u-1)(u-3)&\\le0\\\\u&\\in[1,3].\\end{align*}$$\nThus $1\\le|x|\\le3$: the distance of $x$ from $0$ is between $1$ and $3$, inclusive. Hence\n$$-3\\le x\\le-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad1\\le x\\le3.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
